e  title it all begins with human induced  pluripotent stem cells  these induced pluripotent stem cells are  made using a process known as cellular  reprogramming and so you can take a  human differentiated cell like a skin  cell and turn it into a so-called  pluripotent stem cell which has the  potential to replicate  but also to differentiate into different  cell types  so here they introduce the human-induced  pro-potent stem cells into an  intermediate stage called incipient  mesoderm-like cells and from here they  can be turned into human primordial germ  cell-like cells  so if you remember from the start these  are the cells that make gametes so egg  and sperm  and the like is because they are like  the cells but they're not actually the  cells because that would involve taking  them from a human embryo  okay so hopefully you're still with me  we now have some egg cell precursors  and so to get them to turn into oocytes  they have to somewhat simulate what it  would be like in a growing embryo  so the human primordial gem cell-like  cells are then grown with mouse  embryonic ovarian somatic cells which  enables the formation of reconstituted  ovaries  it then takes around four months for the  human cells to differentiate into the  precursory state for oocytes  a similar strategy has also been  developed to do the same thing to make  precursory sperm cells  this process has been so far taken even  further in mouth systems  where they've gone full circle and used  mouse derived precursory egg cells to  make functional embryos and viable  offspring  the pubs were fertile and remained alive  for at least 11 months but they did  notice however that the placentas of the  pups were heavier than a normal mice and  the pups themselves also tended to be  heavier  moreover the success rate of full-time  development was low at 3.5 percent  compared to in fivo generated oversights  at 61.7  so why  well the thing is germ cells undergo  some quite substantial changes early 